UP|52|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|This was an easy hand to play. BTW, 6@C has plays although pretty unbiddable. In 6@C I can take one spade, 2 diamonds, two hearts, five clubs, and two heart ruff for 12 tricks. There are often slams that make with a good fit that cannot be bid.|
PG| ***** 17 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^^B@2^*BWest: ^*nShould I have lead 7@H?|
PG| ***** 18 ***** |


cp|8|AT|^^
^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|No, the 10 is the correct standard lead, the 9 if you play ^*BCoded 9s^*n (where you lead 9 from A109 K109 or Q109).|
PG| ***** 19 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|^*BCode tens^*n and ^*BCoded nines^*n are slight superior to standard leads but not that important. However, you should be aware of how they work because many people play them.

|
PG| ***** 20 ***** |


