mb|1S|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|Had West passed, I assume North would bid 1@H. But since West overcalled 1@S, now North must make a |CP|1|FP|2|AT|^*Hhttp://www.bridgesights.com/hondobridge/hondoviewer/hondoviewer.php?sf=negativedoubles,Negative Double^*N|CP||FP||at|, which basically is the legal way for North to bid 1@H.|

n#|9|at|^^^fIf you do follow the link you can return  HERE  by clicking the  |fp|1|n#|3|at|@L|fp||n^|3|at|   icon button, top left.|
PG| ***** 23 ***** |


mb|D|mb|2S|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|3C|mb|P|mb|P|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I often will have 5 clubs on this auction but sometimes I might have 4. It is hard for North to know whether to pass or bid 3@D. From the bidding by the opponents and his hand he knows I have a singleton spade (or perhaps even void) making it more likely I am 5-5 or perhaps even 6-5 in the minors. So I don't hate pass.|
PG| ***** 24 ***** |


mb|P|
pg| ***** 25 ***** |


pc|ST|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|This is going to be a tough hand to play. One could claim I should not bid 3@C but with a quality suit (3 honors) I thought it was worth a shot. |
PG| ***** 26 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|I am not sure if 3@D does much better either. But it is easier to play in a 5-2 fit than a 4-3 fit, particularly when you are short in the opponents' suit.|
