mb|3S|nt|^z@3^b@2^^|mb|4H?|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|There are very few hands, when one side has a 9+ card heart fit, and the other side has a 9+ card spade fit where bidding 4@S is wrong over 4@H. In fact it is just about automatic when that situation arises to bid 4@S. On this hand it is very obvious with a singleton heart and favorable vulnerability.|
PG| ***** 107 ***** |


nt|^z@3^b@2^^|cp|8|AT|^B@2^*Bhondo717: ^*N|cp||at|BTW, that is why East might consider not bidding 4@H because it is not clear he wants me to bid 4@S. But it is going to work out okay as it turns out.|
